          "end": 91.61,
          "en": "and you can then choose a name for your Android package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 91.61,
          "end": 95.58,
          "en": "This should be an identifier which has a shape like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 95.58,
          "end": 97.227,
          "en": "basically a reverse URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 98.42,
          "end": 100.39,
          "en": "And this should be a unique identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 100.39,
          "end": 101.7,
          "en": "which is why you typically use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 101.7,
          "end": 105.19,
